Lab patch for Strix 685bbc8 (v1.7.1), applied at image build.

Why: a headless scan that filed any finding exits 2 (strix/interface/main.py 549-552),
which the harness would read as a crash. The lab never passes --fail-on, so the exit
code is kept for errors only; findings are read from the run's own files.

diff --git a/strix/interface/main.py b/strix/interface/main.py
index 846a35da..6c2a6e6b 100644
--- a/strix/interface/main.py
+++ b/strix/interface/main.py
@@ -546,7 +546,9 @@ def main() -> None:
 
     display_completion_message(args, results_path)
 
-    if args.non_interactive:
+    # Lab patch: exit 2 only when --fail-on asks for it. Without the flag a headless
+    # scan that found something exits 2, which reads as a crash, not a finished run.
+    if args.non_interactive and args.fail_on is not None:
         report_state = get_global_report_state()
         if report_state and findings_fail_build(report_state.vulnerability_reports, args.fail_on):
             sys.exit(2)
